# PlaySapien — root _redirects
#
# Audit B3. Sojourner's asset base is './assets/' (partC.js:3), so a request to
# /sojourner WITHOUT the trailing slash resolves every asset against the
# platform root and the globe never loads. Pages normally normalises this; the
# audit calls it the highest-consequence unverified assumption in the move, so
# it is made explicit here rather than assumed.
#
# VERIFY ON FIRST DEPLOY:
#   curl -I https://playsapien.com/sojourner
#   curl -I https://playsapien.com/wordchain
# Both must answer 301 to the slashed form.
#
# More specific rules first — Pages takes the first match. deploy/assemble.sh
# appends each game's _redirects.fragment BELOW these, so a fragment that
# restates one of the rules here is harmless: the platform rule matches first.

# Audit B1 safety net: the shell shipped 'word-chain' as Word Chain's slug for a
# while. Anything already linked that way keeps working.
/word-chain/*   /wordchain/:splat   301
/word-chain     /wordchain/         301

/sojourner      /sojourner/         301
/wordchain      /wordchain/         301
